0,Cora language - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cora_language,"Cora (English: / ˈkoʊrə /) is an indigenous language of Mexico of the Uto-Aztecan language family, spoken by approximately 30,000 people. [2] It is spoken by the ethnic group that is widely known as the Cora, but who refer to themselves as Naáyarite. The Cora inhabit the northern sierra of the Mexican state Nayarit which is named after its indigenous inhabitants. A significant portion of ...","Cora, Santa Teresa",Uto-Aztecan
