4,"Cora language, alphabet and pronunciation - Omniglot",https://www.omniglot.com/writing/cora.htm,"Cora (naáyarite) Cora is an Uto-Aztecan language spoken in the states of Nayarit, Jalisco and Durango in central Mexico. In 2010 there were 20,000 Cora speakers. There are also some Cora speakers in Colorado in the USA. There are two main varieties of Cora: Cora del Nayar or Cora Meseño, and Cora de Santa Teresa or Cora Tereseño.","Cora, Santa Teresa",Uto-Aztecan
5,"Cora language - Alchetron, The Free Social Encyclopedia",https://alchetron.com/Cora-language,Cora is an indigenous language of Mexico of the Uto-Aztecan language family. It is spoken by the ethnic group that is widely known as the Cora but who refer to themselves as Naáyarite. The Cora inhabit the northern sierra of the Mexican state Nayarit which is named after its indigenous inhabitants.,"Cora, Santa Teresa",Uto-Aztecan
